cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "opensidewalks-nyc: an OpenSidewalks v0.3 pedestrian graph of New York City"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite as below."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  An experimental pedestrian network of New York City in the OpenSidewalks
  Schema v0.3, built from OpenStreetMap, the NYC DOT curb ramp survey, NYC
  planimetric sidewalks and LiDAR. Nothing in it has been checked on the
  ground. Dataset version 0.3.4-nyc.1 is this project's own version; it uses
  OpenSidewalks Schema v0.3. opensidewalks-nyc is an independent project by
  Adam Munawar Rahman. It is not made or endorsed by the Taskar Center for
  Accessible Technology, OpenSidewalks or TDEI, nor by NYC DOT or the City of
  New York.
